22658190372 and raw_uniform=0.630259626350387, but is below g3-r0020-pooled_reference=0.6307714974815276. Radius-only target AUC=0.6306798923499843 also fails to beat that reference despite better Logloss. This motivates, but does not prove, a group-allocation explanation: equal weighting may amplify small match groups and offset useful learned within-group evidence. Replace only group prior mass 1/K by n_g/N, keeping each group softmax. Constant scores now reconstruct the global pooled vector. Predicted utility must exceed the new empirical-uniform control, the frozen stronger pooled_reference and both source bests, and survive the empirical-context and historical active duplicated-evidence controls. Query and mass effects may interact; existing equal-mass target/context/uniform cells supply the other factorial level. All prior comparisons are single-seed observations, not established mechanism evidence.',\n  'nearest_work':[\n   {'source_ref':'paper:din; primary arXiv:1706.06978v4, section 4.3 lines 250-277; text_sha256=83fb9eeca31e2fa3c557b6f08b893ad0018cefb33da6e00952136b9ce17e607e','verification':'read','difference':'Inherit candidate-ad-conditioned local relevance and field interaction scoring through the existing adapted baseline. DIN removes softmax to retain interest intensity; this proposal retains normalized within-group softmax and total mass one, fixes group masses to observed fractions, and preserves the full pooled predictor. It is not an exact DIN reproduction or a claim of new attention.'},\n   {'source_ref':'g3-r0019-raw_target; inherited _RawFusionModel in history_g3_r0020_pooled_reference.py; c7afb27541d642ee27bce4d54755406b29a3605d140453a71e8c9087882a123b','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'The candidate inherits every ancestor class verbatim. The final Model overrides only grouped mass allocation and diagnostics; no parameters are allocated. Target/context/uniform keep their original queries, scoring, raw scale and fusion head. Compared with raw_target, the sole mathematical intervention is empirical rather than occupied-group-uniform prior.'},\n   {'source_ref':'g3-r0020-pooled_reference; history_g3_r0020_pooled_reference.py; c7afb27541d642ee27bce4d54755406b29a3605d140453a71e8c9087882a123b','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Its strongest result uses only a duplicated global pooled vector, with scorer contribution and gradients zero. New empirical_uniform reconstructs that vector algebraically with the same allocation and head; target/context enable learned within-group deviations around this nested null. Floating-point reduction and gradient arithmetic differ, so the new null is trained rather than assuming identical checkpoints.'},\n   {'source_ref':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed; history_g1_r0019_pooled_observed.py; ca68bdb11d082057b8c7984e212e745331b2f33d4e8895dc4488efe13ad3ed02','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Retain the complete stronger source representation and residuals; the existing fusion head adds capacity and a readout. The empirical-uniform cell tests that extra capacity using existing evidence; gains over the frozen source alone do not establish target-conditioned complementarity.'},\n   {'source_ref':'g3-r0007-balanced_target; history_g3_r0007_balanced_target.py; ae07cfc238a702f3f917d2376779341d41249be731de3878c1e3b17e6b8545a4','verification':'read','difference':'Retain this frozen target-readout source best as a utility comparator. Its equal match-group mass is examined rather than mandated. The new branch is fitted jointly with the complete stronger pooled representation; cross-architecture performance is not a single-factor mechanism estimate.'},\n   {'source_ref':'queryformer-paper-v1; arXiv:2609.16548v1, lines 175-202; text_sha256=f8e114e22e2e8016610748784b98f2ffb59e5611f92ef03689e11f7aed4de3a6','verification':'read','difference':'Considered query-generation cross attention and packed domain retrieval. Neither new queries, views, domain supervision nor optimization recipe is adopted: local evidence first motivates a mass-allocation control. Source pCVR, item/dense fields and row-group split differ from this task.'},\n   {'source_ref':'paper:dmr; pinned author README at 2c6e76804281954a3c969010a31712cd5054aca9; text_sha256=656c9e5eec79c9843e907a555ede2bf0a66a0db3515916af3d655080057c5a75','verification':'read','difference':'Only README lines 4-8 are verified: category/brand/behavior histories have no item IDs. No item features, retrieval targets or auxiliary labels are introduced. Publisher full text is unavailable; no detailed DMR equivalence or priority claim is made.'}\n  ],\n  'inherited_components':held+[\n   'Exact _ParentModel, _GapParentModel, _ResolutionParentModel, _PooledObservedModel, _NormalizedFusionModel and _RawFusionModel class ASTs from the frozen supplied source; original output and zero-initialized fusion residual retained.',\n   '17,270,691 allocated parameters expected from unchanged constructors; 17,568 in appended head and 4,226 in inherited scorer, to be verified by host. Uniform has the same allocation but a deliberately inactive scorer; effective capacity differs.',\n   'Historical normalized fusion, raw scale, radius-only, query replacement and duplicated-evidence trajectories all retained as evidence. No local execution failure or previous_runtime_error is supplied. Failed scientific contrasts are not execution failures.'\n  ],\n  'proposed_difference':'For group g with n_g valid events and N total, replace w_i=(1/K)*exp(s_i)/sum_{j in g} exp(s_j) by w_i=(n_g/N)*exp(s_i)/sum_{j in g} exp(s_j), with zero mass for empty groups/histories. Each occupied group retains its empirical event fraction regardless of scores, so the candidate learns only within-group relevance. Category and brand retain separate weights and share half of their mass on action/recency values. No learned prior, additional gate, parameter, information, loss or optimizer change. The algebra nests the global pooled null when scores are constant. Newness relative to broader literature remains unverified; this is a mechanism-distinct local allocation replacement.',\n  'predictions':[\n   'Implementation: group weight mass equals n_g/N, masked events have zero mass, nonempty total weight is one; independent per-group loop oracle agrees; uniform summary equals the existing global pool. Empty/zero-length outputs remain finite, singleton readouts equal their pool, and padding/order invariance holds within floating-point tolerance.',\n   'Primary utility prediction: empirical_target exceeds empirical_uniform, g3-r0020-pooled_reference, g1-r0019-pooled_observed (0.6302753100663608) and g3-r0007-balanced_target (0.6202303848951921) on full-population validation ROC-AUC. Report unweighted Logloss separately; an AUC/Logloss tradeoff is not hidden.',\n   'Target-conditioning prediction: empirical_target exceeds empirical_context with equal allocation and measured cost; context changes only query construction and retains target-dependent match partitions. Comparison to uniform is essential to test utility beyond existing evidence.',\n   'Allocation prediction: empirical_target minus g3-r0019-raw_target is positive; compare this with empirical_context minus g3-r0019-raw_context and empirical_uniform minus g3-r0019-raw_uniform. The difference of target-context gaps between prior levels tests interaction; do not infer an allocation mechanism solely from a candidate-source gain.',\n   'Existing history-length, hour, behavior-composition and train-frequency slices are exploratory robustness checks, with their supplied sample/positive/negative counts. The dominant >64-history slice contains 3,026,583 impressions and 151,372 positives; inspect it and small/empty histories without changing global selection or cherry-picking bins. No new frequency or missing-field bins can be fabricated from unavailable raw data.',\n   'Host measures parameters, train and allocated GPU seconds if supplied, wall time, peak memory, examples processed if supplied, inference throughput and batch p50/p95 latency. This replacement predicts no meaningful complexity increase; any equal-compute efficiency claim requires measured cost, not matched recipe alone.'\n  ],\n  'falsifiers':[\n   'Reject implementation validity if per-group mass or uniform-to-global-pool identity fails beyond numerical tolerance, or outputs/diagnostics are nonfinite. Record failed receipt and cost before any corrected proposal; do not launch a duplicate unknown-state run.',\n   'If empirical_target does not improve over empirical_uniform and the stronger pooled_reference, incremental utility is unsupported even if it exceeds both original source bests.',\n   'If empirical_context matches the candidate, target-query-specific explanation is unsupported; retained target-defined grouping prevents claiming a fully target-independent control.',\n   'If allocation helps uniform/context as much as target, it supports distribution weighting or optimization rather than target-conditioned complementarity; compare the full prior-by-query contrasts.',\n   'If the historical active duplicated-evidence control g3-r0019-raw_pooled_duplicate or the exact pooled null explains the gain, capacity/recombination remains a sufficient explanation. The active duplicate has different granularity and cost, so its failure alone cannot establish mechanism.',\n   'If effects reverse across paired seeds or paired user-cluster uncertainty includes no gain, retain preliminary/null status. One seed or checkpoint sensitivity cannot establish a mechanism or significance.',\n   'If quality gains require materially more measured compute or worsen Logloss, report the tradeoff; do not claim simultaneous accuracy and efficiency improvement.'\n  ],\n  'alternative_explanations':[\n   'All observed AUC differences are small single-seed results subject to checkpoint selection, rounding, shared-validation adaptation and training variance. The same seed and data order do not eliminate these risks.',\n   'Pooled_reference already outperforms raw_target, while radius_target has better Logloss; neither raw direction nor scalar norm has demonstrated unique predictive sufficiency. Added nonlinear readout capacity and changed optimization can explain gains over the original pooled source.',\n   'The empirical prior also reduces minority match-group amplification; benefits may reflect regularization or population composition rather than improved semantic retrieval. This proposal does not assume rare groups are noisy without measuring them.',\n   'Context queries ignore current-target embeddings only at query construction. All learned cells still use target-dependent match membership and static features. Uniform empirical weights cancel this grouping algebraically, but the complete classifier still receives target fields.',\n   'An active duplicated-evidence control has equal allocated scorer capacity but different softmax support and event granularity, and is faster. It is complementary evidence, not a perfect isolation of active event-level attention capacity.',\n   'Synthetic witness separation and checkpoint substitution are implementation/sensitivity checks, not a causal estimate of predictive benefit. Diagnostic coverage is only the first 512 validation impressions.',\n   'Static snapshot as-of dates are undocumented. Inputs lack item IDs and the supplied history is truncated to 128. Validation-only findings do not establish production point-in-time or held-out test generalization.'\n  ],\n  'contrasts':[\n   {'parent_ref':'g3-r0019-raw_target','intervention':'empirical_target: change only within-readout group mass from 1/K to n_g/N','control':'Existing g3-r0019-raw_target with equal occupied-group masses','held_fixed':held,'remaining_confounds':['Historical execution timing and numerical nondeterminism; both seed 42, no repeated support yet','This source is below the stronger pooled_reference; beating it alone is insufficient'], 'decision_if_supported':'Inspect context and uniform allocation effects; repeat candidate versus closest pooled and query controls before attribution.','decision_if_not_supported':'Do not claim empirical group weighting improves target retrieval. Retain null and assess whether pooled capacity remains preferable.'},\n   {'parent_ref':'g3-r0020-pooled_reference','intervention':'empirical_target: learned within-group retrieval under fixed empirical masses','control':'New empirical_uniform: same full module and score graph, scores multiplied by zero; summary mathematically equals global pool. Also retain frozen g3-r0020-pooled_reference.','held_fixed':held,'remaining_confounds':['Uniform retains allocated but not active scorer capacity','Equivalent pooled functions can train differently through finite-precision reductions; no exact checkpoint equality asserted','Target and uniform have different nonzero backward work, so measured cost may differ'], 'decision_if_supported':'Only consider incremental predictive utility if stronger pooled_reference and both source bests are also exceeded; then compare active context and duplicate controls.','decision_if_not_supported':'Prefer stronger pooled evidence control; no complementarity claim regardless of gains against weaker baselines.'},\n   {'parent_ref':'g3-r0019-raw_context','intervention':'empirical_target uses current category/brand embeddings as separate queries','control':'New empirical_context uses history category/brand means as separate queries; same empirical masses and all target-dependent groups. Existing g3-r0019-raw_context is the equal-mass counterpart.','held_fixed':held,'remaining_confounds':['Only query construction is target-independent; match groups and shared classifier remain target-dependent','Training dynamics and query distribution differ despite identical capacity'], 'decision_if_supported':'Compare target-context gaps across empirical and historical balanced priors, then seek paired repeated support.','decision_if_not_supported':'Target-specific query explanation fails under this allocation, even if learned context retrieval has utility.'},\n   {'parent_ref':'g3-r0019-raw_uniform','intervention':'Prior-by-query factorial completed with empirical_target, empirical_context, empirical_uniform','control':'Historical equal-prior cells g3-r0019-raw_target, g3-r0019-raw_context, g3-r0019-raw_uniform; historical active existing-evidence g3-r0019-raw_pooled_duplicate as additional capacity control','held_fixed':held,'remaining_confounds':['Three historical cells and three new cells are matched by protocol and inherited source, but not execution time','Active duplicate changes support from events to group summaries and measured cost; cannot equate this with frequency-preserving attention','Repeated random initializations assess stability, not additional mechanism contrasts'], 'decision_if_supported':'Report query main effect, prior main effect and difference of target-context gaps. Reserve repetition for the consequential contrasts; retain both source bests as utility controls.','decision_if_not_supported':'Document that group-prior replacement failed to resolve redundancy. Next falsifiable question is whether target-specific fine associations add utility to the best pooled-capacity predictor under a different controlled readout, not a broad refutation of attention.'}\n  ],\n  'cost_plan':{\n   'estimate_ref':'run://r-001 context.remaining_seconds=11132.827180147171, trial cap=1760.9324324010606; measured full-unit walls: g3-r0019-raw_target 1055.4190s, raw_context 1013.5588s, raw_uniform 1033.4558s; g3-r0020-pooled_reference 1038.7963s. Use 1100s planning/unit rather than obsolete 704s original baseline estimate.',\n   'all_variants_counted':True,\n   'attribution_reserve':'Three registered full-protocol variants, including both controls, expected 3300s total (worst case three trial caps=5282.7973s). No local training, subset screen, calibration or extra forward jobs. All source retrieval, coding, diagnostics, failed execution and host scoring remain charged. The six-cell prior-by-query design reuses committed equal-mass controls with exact inherited class AST verification. This is not a claim of independently replicated evidence.',\n   'assessment_reserve':'Nominal remainder after new variants is 7832.8272s before preparation/other charges. Provisionally reserve 6600s for seeds 43 and 44 on the selected candidate, empirical_context and empirical_uniform (six full units), with seed42 supplied by this round. At nominal cost this leaves 1232.8272s for preparation/diagnostics/failures/overrun. Final comparator suite must include both frozen source bests, strongest pooled_reference, raw_target and active duplicate at least as existing seed42 receipts; rerun more source seeds only if actual remaining budget permits. Freeze source/config hashes, selected validation comparisons and seed suite before final host repetitions. No test or closed-archive inputs are authorized.',\n   'stop_rule':'Treat the host ledger and per-trial cap as hard limits; never raise them. Recheck remaining budget after every receipt, including preparation/failure charges, and prioritize final attribution repetitions over new directions. If actual unit costs approach the cap, the nominal six-run repetition reserve cannot hold: reduce optional scope and disclose omitted seeds, not budget. Stop immediately for nonfinite/contract-invalid behavior or unknown execution state pending a receipt. Do not retry an unknown-state job. If no useful admissible comparison fits, preserve the incumbent and report preliminary/null evidence. A poor empirical_target may still justify its two predeclared controls to distinguish allocation failure from query redundancy; no automatic second architecture sweep.'\n  }\n },\n 'variants':[],\n 'knowledge_assessments':[],\n 'local_validation':{\n  'status':'syntax_and_source_checks_only',\n  'checks':['All three modules parsed and compiled in memory without importing Torch.','All seven inherited class ASTs are exactly equal to the supplied frozen pooled_reference module; final subclass allocates zero additional parameters.','Imports restricted to torch and math; model code contains no filesystem/network access.','Independent pure-Python scalar specification oracle: 210 cases, lengths 0/1/2/4/17/64/128, logits in [-1000,1000]; nonnegative finite weights, empirical group masses, total mass, uniform=global mean, padding/reordering and singleton/empty conditions passed. Largest scalar uniform-pool error=4.440892098500626e-16. This checks algebra, not Torch implementation.'],\n  'not_executed':['Torch forward/backward','Host diagnostics','Training and scoring','New seed comparisons','User-cluster bootstrap: only host-authorized predictions/cluster interface may be used, none supplied in this phase'],\n  'host_execution':'Host automatically loads each standalone Model(meta, config) and runs the frozen protocol from proposal.json. No training executable or data path is exposed locally, so no invented direct-training command is supplied.'\n },\n 'scene_observations':[\n  {'maturity':'local_observation','refs':['g3-r0018-fusion_target','g3-r0018-fusion_context','g3-r0018-fusion_uniform','g3-r0018-fusion_pooled_duplicate'],'observation':'Normalized fusion target has AUC 0.63037146, context 0.63030728, uniform 0.63033338, active duplicate 0.63026404. These small differences did not establish complementarity.','provisional_explanation':'Shared pooled ancestry and norm normalization may obscure incremental evidence; not controlled support for a unique mechanism.'},\n  {'maturity':'local_observation','refs':['g3-r0019-raw_target','g3-r0019-raw_context','g3-r0019-raw_uniform','g3-r0019-raw_pooled_duplicate'],'observation':'Retaining magnitude improved target AUC to 0.63072032; target-context gap 0.00033806. Raw uniform and active duplicate remain lower.','provisional_explanation':'Magnitude is consequential in this implementation, but changing effective features and training can explain the gain. No sufficiency or novelty established.'},\n  {'maturity':'local_observation','refs':['g3-r0020-radius_target','g3-r0020-radius_context','g3-r0020-pooled_reference'],'observation':'Radius target AUC 0.63067989/Logloss 0.19262051; context AUC 0.63025376; pure pooled AUC 0.63077150/Logloss 0.19264156. Raw direction is not shown necessary, scalar sufficiency is not established, and target incremental AUC over pooled remains unsupported.','provisional_explanation':'Capacity/recombination of already available pooled evidence remains sufficient to explain the incumbent. Revise the prior interpretation rather than erasing it.'},\n  {'maturity':'hypothesis','refs':['g3-r0019-raw_uniform','g3-r0020-pooled_reference'],'observation':'Source inspection shows raw_uniform is equal across occupied groups and pooled_reference is equal across valid events; these are different nulls for imbalanced group sizes.','provisional_explanation':'Preserving empirical group fractions may remove a distribution distortion while allowing useful learned within-group attention. The proposed controls can falsify this; no new measured outcome exists.'}\n ]\n}\nfor name,file,role,note in [\n ('empirical_target','candidate.py','candidate','Observed-fraction group masses with target category/brand queries; raw readout and complete pooled predictor unchanged.'),\n ('empirical_context','candidate_context.py','control','Replace only target query by history-field mean query; same empirical group masses and allocated active scorer capacity. Match groups still depend on the target.'),\n ('empirical_uniform','candidate_uniform.py','control','Scores multiplied by zero; empirical group masses make readout algebraically equal to the global pooled vector. Same allocated capacity; scorer gradient is zero. Checks the stronger pooled null and finite-precision training differences.')]:\n text=Path(file).read_text(); tree=ast.parse(text)\n config=ast.literal_eval(next(n.value for n in tree.body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='CONFIG' for t in n.targets)))\n proposal['variants'].append({'name':name,'file':file,'role':role,'config':config,'note':note+' Source SHA256='+hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest()+'. Syntax, inherited AST and independent scalar algebra checks passed; Torch execution and empirical results pending host. No new performance or priority claim.'})\nfor kid,decision,reason in [\n ('taac2026-academic-1-craft','considered','Supplied card and inherited usage reviewed. No local propagation-instability or reliable-context evidence justifies a transport gate; no source architecture adopted.'),\n ('taac2026-academic-2-unidac','rejected','Organizer-summary detail only; no separate older-history information or dual-domain exchange is needed for the observed prior-mass mismatch. No unavailable inputs or compressed-history path assumed.'),\n ('taac2026-academic-3-unitokenformer','rejected','Organizer-summary detail only; no local token bottleneck established. Token allocation would change capacity and compute alongside the prior intervention.'),\n ('taac2026-industry-1-queryformer','considered','Primary v1 lines 175-202 read; generated query probes and packed domain retrieval differ from the present fixed-query, within-group prior contrast. Source conversion labels, dense/item features and row-group split are not transferred.'),\n ('taac2026-industry-2-unidot','considered','Supplied card and inherited usage reviewed; its reported AUC/Logloss disagreement reinforces separate metric reporting. No local evidence requires additional highway interactions, buses or losses.'),\n ('paper:din','used','Primary v4 section 4.3 read; inherited target-conditioned relevance is examined using a nested empirical-pooling null. The paper motivates conditioning/intensity but does not establish local benefit or this group-prior choice.'),\n ('paper:dmr','unresolved','Pinned author README read and no-item field boundary retained. Full publisher text remains unavailable; detailed architectural comparison and priority are unresolved.')]:\n proposal['knowledge_assessments'].append({\n  'knowledge_id':kid,'decision':decision,'rationale':reason,\n  'transformed_mechanism':'Inherited local relevance scorer; replace occupied-group-uniform mass by observed event fractions, retaining softmax and the complete pooled predictor.' if kid=='paper:din' else 'No new source architecture adopted in this intervention.',\n  'variant_names':['empirical_target','empirical_context','empirical_uniform'] if kid=='paper:din' else [],\n  'nearest_work_difference':'Fixed empirical group masses, no extra parameter/query/view, capacity-matched pooled null and query replacement. Not unnormalized DIN or a reproduction of industry architectures; broader novelty unverified.',\n  'falsifier':'Target readout fails to exceed new empirical-uniform and strongest frozen pooled control, or its gain is matched by the history-query/duplicated-evidence control or reverses under paired repetition.'\n })\nPath('proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(proposal,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Wrote proposal.json with',len(proposal['variants']),'variants,',len(proposal['study']['contrasts']),'contrasts,',len(proposal['knowledge_assessments']),'knowledge assessments.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport ast, hashlib, json\nprotocol='9c1635366a72f4c4f67708ee7ae9b72a1b90197ffed3485736388ceff7c91d3e'\nheld=['Frozen protocol '+protocol,'Same visible static category/brand fields and causal history prefixes; history_limit=128','Three epochs, all first-six-day exposures, natural prevalence, batch_size=4096','Scratch initialization and paired host seed 42; final paired seeds 42/43/44 when feasible','Identical embeddings, scorer, head widths, parameter allocation order and initialization draws','Raw readout, match partitions, separate category/brand queries and values, inherited pooled predictor and all auxiliary residuals','Unchanged Adam/lr=0.001, loss, label access, scorer and validation population']\nproposal={\n 'parent_trial':'g3-r0020-pooled_reference',\n 'study':{\n  'id':'g3-empirical-group-mass-readout',\n  'protocol_ref':protocol,\n  'evidence_refs':['baseline-static','baseline-pooled','baseline-din','g1-r0019-pooled_observed','g3-r0007-balanced_target','g3-r0018-fusion_target','g3-r0018-fusion_context','g3-r0018-fusion_uniform','g3-r0018-fusion_pooled_duplicate','g3-r0019-raw_target','g3-r0019-raw_context','g3-r0019-raw_uniform','g3-r0019-raw_pooled_duplicate','g3-r0020-radius_target','g3-r0020-radius_context','g3-r0020-pooled_reference'],\n  'question':'Does retaining observed match-group event proportions during within-group target-conditioned retrieval expose incremental utility beyond the stronger global pooled-capacity control, both frozen source bests, and a query-only target-independent replacement?',\n  'hypothesis':'Observed limitation: equal mass per occupied match group is not the empirical event distribution. Thus the previous raw-uniform readout is a mean of group means, whereas the current pooled_reference is an event-weighted mean. g3-r0019-raw_target AUC=0.6307203236894126 beats raw_context=0.6303822658190372 and raw_uniform=0.630259626350387, but is below g3-r0020-pooled_reference=0.6307714974815276. Radius-only target AUC=0.6306798923499843 also fails to beat that reference despite better Logloss. This motivates, but does not prove, a group-allocation explanation: equal weighting may amplify small match groups and offset useful learned within-group evidence. Replace only group prior mass 1/K by n_g/N, keeping each group softmax. Constant scores now reconstruct the global pooled vector. Predicted utility must exceed the new empirical-uniform control, the frozen stronger pooled_reference and both source bests, and survive the empirical-context and historical active duplicated-evidence controls. Query and mass effects may interact; existing equal-mass target/context/uniform cells supply the other factorial level. All prior comparisons are single-seed observations, not established mechanism evidence.',\n  'nearest_work':[\n   {'source_ref':'paper:din; primary arXiv:1706.06978v4, section 4.3 lines 250-277; text_sha256=83fb9eeca31e2fa3c557b6f08b893ad0018cefb33da6e00952136b9ce17e607e','verification':'read','difference':'Inherit candidate-ad-conditioned local relevance and field interaction scoring through the existing adapted baseline. DIN removes softmax to retain interest intensity; this proposal retains normalized within-group softmax and total mass one, fixes group masses to observed fractions, and preserves the full pooled predictor. It is not an exact DIN reproduction or a claim of new attention.'},\n   {'source_ref':'g3-r0019-raw_target; inherited _RawFusionModel in history_g3_r0020_pooled_reference.py; c7afb27541d642ee27bce4d54755406b29a3605d140453a71e8c9087882a123b','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'The candidate inherits every ancestor class verbatim. The final Model overrides only grouped mass allocation and diagnostics; no parameters are allocated. Target/context/uniform keep their original queries, scoring, raw scale and fusion head. Compared with raw_target, the sole mathematical intervention is empirical rather than occupied-group-uniform prior.'},\n   {'source_ref':'g3-r0020-pooled_reference; history_g3_r0020_pooled_reference.py; c7afb27541d642ee27bce4d54755406b29a3605d140453a71e8c9087882a123b','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Its strongest result uses only a duplicated global pooled vector, with scorer contribution and gradients zero. New empirical_uniform reconstructs that vector algebraically with the same allocation and head; target/context enable learned within-group deviations around this nested null. Floating-point reduction and gradient arithmetic differ, so the new null is trained rather than assuming identical checkpoints.'},\n   {'source_ref':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed; history_g1_r0019_pooled_observed.py; ca68bdb11d082057b8c7984e212e745331b2f33d4e8895dc4488efe13ad3ed02','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Retain the complete stronger source representation and residuals; the existing fusion head adds capacity and a readout. The empirical-uniform cell tests that extra capacity using existing evidence; gains over the frozen source alone do not establish target-conditioned complementarity.'},\n   {'source_ref':'g3-r0007-balanced_target; history_g3_r0007_balanced_target.py; ae07cfc238a702f3f917d2376779341d41249be731de3878c1e3b17e6b8545a4','verification':'read','difference':'Retain this frozen target-readout source best as a utility comparator. Its equal match-group mass is examined rather than mandated. The new branch is fitted jointly with the complete stronger pooled representation; cross-architecture performance is not a single-factor mechanism estimate.'},\n   {'source_ref':'queryformer-paper-v1; arXiv:2609.16548v1, lines 175-202; text_sha256=f8e114e22e2e8016610748784b98f2ffb59e5611f92ef03689e11f7aed4de3a6','verification':'read','difference':'Considered query-generation cross attention and packed domain retrieval. Neither new queries, views, domain supervision nor optimization recipe is adopted: local evidence first motivates a mass-allocation control. Source pCVR, item/dense fields and row-group split differ from this task.'},\n   {'source_ref':'paper:dmr; pinned author README at 2c6e76804281954a3c969010a31712cd5054aca9; text_sha256=656c9e5eec79c9843e907a555ede2bf0a66a0db3515916af3d655080057c5a75','verification':'read','difference':'Only README lines 4-8 are verified: category/brand/behavior histories have no item IDs. No item features, retrieval targets or auxiliary labels are introduced. Publisher full text is unavailable; no detailed DMR equivalence or priority claim is made.'}\n  ],\n  'inherited_components':held+[\n   'Exact _ParentModel, _GapParentModel, _ResolutionParentModel, _PooledObservedModel, _NormalizedFusionModel and _RawFusionModel class ASTs from the frozen supplied source; original output and zero-initialized fusion residual retained.',\n   '17,270,691 allocated parameters expected from unchanged constructors; 17,568 in appended head and 4,226 in inherited scorer, to be verified by host. Uniform has the same allocation but a deliberately inactive scorer; effective capacity differs.',\n   'Historical normalized fusion, raw scale, radius-only, query replacement and duplicated-evidence trajectories all retained as evidence. No local execution failure or previous_runtime_error is supplied. Failed scientific contrasts are not execution failures.'\n  ],\n  'proposed_difference':'For group g with n_g valid events and N total, replace w_i=(1/K)*exp(s_i)/sum_{j in g} exp(s_j) by w_i=(n_g/N)*exp(s_i)/sum_{j in g} exp(s_j), with zero mass for empty groups/histories. Each occupied group retains its empirical event fraction regardless of scores, so the candidate learns only within-group relevance. Category and brand retain separate weights and share half of their mass on action/recency values. No learned prior, additional gate, parameter, information, loss or optimizer change. The algebra nests the global pooled null when scores are constant. Newness relative to broader literature remains unverified; this is a mechanism-distinct local allocation replacement.',\n  'predictions':[\n   'Implementation: group weight mass equals n_g/N, masked events have zero mass, nonempty total weight is one; independent per-group loop oracle agrees; uniform summary equals the existing global pool. Empty/zero-length outputs remain finite, singleton readouts equal their pool, and padding/order invariance holds within floating-point tolerance.',\n   'Primary utility prediction: empirical_target exceeds empirical_uniform, g3-r0020-pooled_reference, g1-r0019-pooled_observed (0.6302753100663608) and g3-r0007-balanced_target (0.6202303848951921) on full-population validation ROC-AUC. Report unweighted Logloss separately; an AUC/Logloss tradeoff is not hidden.',\n   'Target-conditioning prediction: empirical_target exceeds empirical_context with equal allocation and measured cost; context changes only query construction and retains target-dependent match partitions. Comparison to uniform is essential to test utility beyond existing evidence.',\n   'Allocation prediction: empirical_target minus g3-r0019-raw_target is positive; compare this with empirical_context minus g3-r0019-raw_context and empirical_uniform minus g3-r0019-raw_uniform. The difference of target-context gaps between prior levels tests interaction; do not infer an allocation mechanism solely from a candidate-source gain.',\n   'Existing history-length, hour, behavior-composition and train-frequency slices are exploratory robustness checks, with their supplied sample/positive/negative counts. The dominant >64-history slice contains 3,026,583 impressions and 151,372 positives; inspect it and small/empty histories without changing global selection or cherry-picking bins. No new frequency or missing-field bins can be fabricated from unavailable raw data.',\n   'Host measures parameters, train and allocated GPU seconds if supplied, wall time, peak memory, examples processed if supplied, inference throughput and batch p50/p95 latency. This replacement predicts no meaningful complexity increase; any equal-compute efficiency claim requires measured cost, not matched recipe alone.'\n  ],\n  'falsifiers':[\n   'Reject implementation validity if per-group mass or uniform-to-global-pool identity fails beyond numerical tolerance, or outputs/diagnostics are nonfinite. Record failed receipt and cost before any corrected proposal; do not launch a duplicate unknown-state run.',\n   'If empirical_target does not improve over empirical_uniform and the stronger pooled_reference, incremental utility is unsupported even if it exceeds both original source bests.',\n   'If empirical_context matches the candidate, target-query-specific explanation is unsupported; retained target-defined grouping prevents claiming a fully target-independent control.',\n   'If allocation helps uniform/context as much as target, it supports distribution weighting or optimization rather than target-conditioned complementarity; compare the full prior-by-query contrasts.',\n   'If the historical active duplicated-evidence control g3-r0019-raw_pooled_duplicate or the exact pooled null explains the gain, capacity/recombination remains a sufficient explanation. The active duplicate has different granularity and cost, so its failure alone cannot establish mechanism.',\n   'If effects reverse across paired seeds or paired user-cluster uncertainty includes no gain, retain preliminary/null status. One seed or checkpoint sensitivity cannot establish a mechanism or significance.',\n   'If quality gains require materially more measured compute or worsen Logloss, report the tradeoff; do not claim simultaneous accuracy and efficiency improvement.'\n  ],\n  'alternative_explanations':[\n   'All observed AUC differences are small single-seed results subject to checkpoint selection, rounding, shared-validation adaptation and training variance. The same seed and data order do not eliminate these risks.',\n   'Pooled_reference already outperforms raw_target, while radius_target has better Logloss; neither raw direction nor scalar norm has demonstrated unique predictive sufficiency. Added nonlinear readout capacity and changed optimization can explain gains over the original pooled source.',\n   'The empirical prior also reduces minority match-group amplification; benefits may reflect regularization or population composition rather than improved semantic retrieval. This proposal does not assume rare groups are noisy without measuring them.',\n   'Context queries ignore current-target embeddings only at query construction. All learned cells still use target-dependent match membership and static features. Uniform empirical weights cancel this grouping algebraically, but the complete classifier still receives target fields.',\n   'An active duplicated-evidence control has equal allocated scorer capacity but different softmax support and event granularity, and is faster. It is complementary evidence, not a perfect isolation of active event-level attention capacity.',\n   'Synthetic witness separation and checkpoint substitution are implementation/sensitivity checks, not a causal estimate of predictive benefit. Diagnostic coverage is only the first 512 validation impressions.',\n   'Static snapshot as-of dates are undocumented. Inputs lack item IDs and the supplied history is truncated to 128. Validation-only findings do not establish production point-in-time or held-out test generalization.'\n  ],\n  'contrasts':[\n   {'parent_ref':'g3-r0019-raw_target','intervention':'empirical_target: change only within-readout group mass from 1/K to n_g/N','control':'Existing g3-r0019-raw_target with equal occupied-group masses','held_fixed':held,'remaining_confounds':['Historical execution timing and numerical nondeterminism; both seed 42, no repeated support yet','This source is below the stronger pooled_reference; beating it alone is insufficient'], 'decision_if_supported':'Inspect context and uniform allocation effects; repeat candidate versus closest pooled and query controls before attribution.','decision_if_not_supported':'Do not claim empirical group weighting improves target retrieval. Retain null and assess whether pooled capacity remains preferable.'},\n   {'parent_ref':'g3-r0020-pooled_reference','intervention':'empirical_target: learned within-group retrieval under fixed empirical masses','control':'New empirical_uniform: same full module and score graph, scores multiplied by zero; summary mathematically equals global pool. Also retain frozen g3-r0020-pooled_reference.','held_fixed':held,'remaining_confounds':['Uniform retains allocated but not active scorer capacity','Equivalent pooled functions can train differently through finite-precision reductions; no exact checkpoint equality asserted','Target and uniform have different nonzero backward work, so measured cost may differ'], 'decision_if_supported':'Only consider incremental predictive utility if stronger pooled_reference and both source bests are also exceeded; then compare active context and duplicate controls.','decision_if_not_supported':'Prefer stronger pooled evidence control; no complementarity claim regardless of gains against weaker baselines.'},\n   {'parent_ref':'g3-r0019-raw_context','intervention':'empirical_target uses current category/brand embeddings as separate queries','control':'New empirical_context uses history category/brand means as separate queries; same empirical masses and all target-dependent groups. Existing g3-r0019-raw_context is the equal-mass counterpart.','held_fixed':held,'remaining_confounds':['Only query construction is target-independent; match groups and shared classifier remain target-dependent','Training dynamics and query distribution differ despite identical capacity'], 'decision_if_supported':'Compare target-context gaps across empirical and historical balanced priors, then seek paired repeated support.','decision_if_not_supported':'Target-specific query explanation fails under this allocation, even if learned context retrieval has utility.'},\n   {'parent_ref':'g3-r0019-raw_uniform','intervention':'Prior-by-query factorial completed with empirical_target, empirical_context, empirical_uniform','control':'Historical equal-prior cells g3-r0019-raw_target, g3-r0019-raw_context, g3-r0019-raw_uniform; historical active existing-evidence g3-r0019-raw_pooled_duplicate as additional capacity control','held_fixed':held,'remaining_confounds':['Three historical cells and three new cells are matched by protocol and inherited source, but not execution time','Active duplicate changes support from events to group summaries and measured cost; cannot equate this with frequency-preserving attention','Repeated random initializations assess stability, not additional mechanism contrasts'], 'decision_if_supported':'Report query main effect, prior main effect and difference of target-context gaps. Reserve repetition for the consequential contrasts; retain both source bests as utility controls.','decision_if_not_supported':'Document that group-prior replacement failed to resolve redundancy. Next falsifiable question is whether target-specific fine associations add utility to the best pooled-capacity predictor under a different controlled readout, not a broad refutation of attention.'}\n  ],\n  'cost_plan':{\n   'estimate_ref':'run://r-001 context.remaining_seconds=11132.827180147171, trial cap=1760.9324324010606; measured full-unit walls: g3-r0019-raw_target 1055.4190s, raw_context 1013.5588s, raw_uniform 1033.4558s; g3-r0020-pooled_reference 1038.7963s. Use 1100s planning/unit rather than obsolete 704s original baseline estimate.',\n   'all_variants_counted':True,\n   'attribution_reserve':'Three registered full-protocol variants, including both controls, expected 3300s total (worst case three trial caps=5282.7973s). No local training, subset screen, calibration or extra forward jobs. All source retrieval, coding, diagnostics, failed execution and host scoring remain charged. The six-cell prior-by-query design reuses committed equal-mass controls with exact inherited class AST verification. This is not a claim of independently replicated evidence.',\n   'assessment_reserve':'Nominal remainder after new variants is 7832.8272s before preparation/other charges. Provisionally reserve 6600s for seeds 43 and 44 on the selected candidate, empirical_context and empirical_uniform (six full units), with seed42 supplied by this round. At nominal cost this leaves 1232.8272s for preparation/diagnostics/failures/overrun. Final comparator suite must include both frozen source bests, strongest pooled_reference, raw_target and active duplicate at least as existing seed42 receipts; rerun more source seeds only if actual remaining budget permits. Freeze source/config hashes, selected validation comparisons and seed suite before final host repetitions. No test or closed-archive inputs are authorized.',\n   'stop_rule':'Treat the host ledger and per-trial cap as hard limits; never raise them. Recheck remaining budget after every receipt, including preparation/failure charges, and prioritize final attribution repetitions over new directions. If actual unit costs approach the cap, the nominal six-run repetition reserve cannot hold: reduce optional scope and disclose omitted seeds, not budget. Stop immediately for nonfinite/contract-invalid behavior or unknown execution state pending a receipt. Do not retry an unknown-state job. If no useful admissible comparison fits, preserve the incumbent and report preliminary/null evidence. A poor empirical_target may still justify its two predeclared controls to distinguish allocation failure from query redundancy; no automatic second architecture sweep.'\n  }\n },\n 'variants':[],\n 'knowledge_assessments':[],\n 'local_validation':{\n  'status':'syntax_and_source_checks_only',\n  'checks':['All three modules parsed and compiled in memory without importing Torch.','All seven inherited class ASTs are exactly equal to the supplied frozen pooled_reference module; final subclass allocates zero additional parameters.','Imports restricted to torch and math; model code contains no filesystem/network access.','Independent pure-Python scalar specification oracle: 210 cases, lengths 0/1/2/4/17/64/128, logits in [-1000,1000]; nonnegative finite weights, empirical group masses, total mass, uniform=global mean, padding/reordering and singleton/empty conditions passed. Largest scalar uniform-pool error=4.440892098500626e-16. This checks algebra, not Torch implementation.'],\n  'not_executed':['Torch forward/backward','Host diagnostics','Training and scoring','New seed comparisons','User-cluster bootstrap: only host-authorized predictions/cluster interface may be used, none supplied in this phase'],\n  'host_execution':'Host automatically loads each standalone Model(meta, config) and runs the frozen protocol from proposal.json. No training executable or data path is exposed locally, so no invented direct-training command is supplied.'\n },\n 'scene_observations':[\n  {'maturity':'local_observation','refs':['g3-r0018-fusion_target','g3-r0018-fusion_context','g3-r0018-fusion_uniform','g3-r0018-fusion_pooled_duplicate'],'observation':'Normalized fusion target has AUC 0.63037146, context 0.63030728, uniform 0.63033338, active duplicate 0.63026404. These small differences did not establish complementarity.','provisional_explanation':'Shared pooled ancestry and norm normalization may obscure incremental evidence; not controlled support for a unique mechanism.'},\n  {'maturity':'local_observation','refs':['g3-r0019-raw_target','g3-r0019-raw_context','g3-r0019-raw_uniform','g3-r0019-raw_pooled_duplicate'],'observation':'Retaining magnitude improved target AUC to 0.63072032; target-context gap 0.00033806. Raw uniform and active duplicate remain lower.','provisional_explanation':'Magnitude is consequential in this implementation, but changing effective features and training can explain the gain. No sufficiency or novelty established.'},\n  {'maturity':'local_observation','refs':['g3-r0020-radius_target','g3-r0020-radius_context','g3-r0020-pooled_reference'],'observation':'Radius target AUC 0.63067989/Logloss 0.19262051; context AUC 0.63025376; pure pooled AUC 0.63077150/Logloss 0.19264156. Raw direction is not shown necessary, scalar sufficiency is not established, and target incremental AUC over pooled remains unsupported.','provisional_explanation':'Capacity/recombination of already available pooled evidence remains sufficient to explain the incumbent. Revise the prior interpretation rather than erasing it.'},\n  {'maturity':'hypothesis','refs':['g3-r0019-raw_uniform','g3-r0020-pooled_reference'],'observation':'Source inspection shows raw_uniform is equal across occupied groups and pooled_reference is equal across valid events; these are different nulls for imbalanced group sizes.','provisional_explanation':'Preserving empirical group fractions may remove a distribution distortion while allowing useful learned within-group attention. The proposed controls can falsify this; no new measured outcome exists.'}\n ]\n}\nfor name,file,role,note in [\n ('empirical_target','candidate.py','candidate','Observed-fraction group masses with target category/brand queries; raw readout and complete pooled predictor unchanged.'),\n ('empirical_context','candidate_context.py','control','Replace only target query by history-field mean query; same empirical group masses and allocated active scorer capacity. Match groups still depend on the target.'),\n ('empirical_uniform','candidate_uniform.py','control','Scores multiplied by zero; empirical group masses make readout algebraically equal to the global pooled vector. Same allocated capacity; scorer gradient is zero. Checks the stronger pooled null and finite-precision training differences.')]:\n text=Path(file).read_text(); tree=ast.parse(text)\n config=ast.literal_eval(next(n.value for n in tree.body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='CONFIG' for t in n.targets)))\n proposal['variants'].append({'name':name,'file':file,'role':role,'config':config,'note':note+' Source SHA256='+hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest()+'. Syntax, inherited AST and independent scalar algebra checks passed; Torch execution and empirical results pending host. No new performance or priority claim.'})\nfor kid,decision,reason in [\n ('taac2026-academic-1-craft','considered','Supplied card and inherited usage reviewed. No local propagation-instability or reliable-context evidence justifies a transport gate; no source architecture adopted.'),\n ('taac2026-academic-2-unidac','rejected','Organizer-summary detail only; no separate older-history information or dual-domain exchange is needed for the observed prior-mass mismatch. No unavailable inputs or compressed-history path assumed.'),\n ('taac2026-academic-3-unitokenformer','rejected','Organizer-summary detail only; no local token bottleneck established. Token allocation would change capacity and compute alongside the prior intervention.'),\n ('taac2026-industry-1-queryformer','considered','Primary v1 lines 175-202 read; generated query probes and packed domain retrieval differ from the present fixed-query, within-group prior contrast. Source conversion labels, dense/item features and row-group split are not transferred.'),\n ('taac2026-industry-2-unidot','considered','Supplied card and inherited usage reviewed; its reported AUC/Logloss disagreement reinforces separate metric reporting. No local evidence requires additional highway interactions, buses or losses.'),\n ('paper:din','used','Primary v4 section 4.3 read; inherited target-conditioned relevance is examined using a nested empirical-pooling null. The paper motivates conditioning/intensity but does not establish local benefit or this group-prior choice.'),\n ('paper:dmr','unresolved','Pinned author README read and no-item field boundary retained. Full publisher text remains unavailable; detailed architectural comparison and priority are unresolved.')]:\n proposal['knowledge_assessments'].append({\n  'knowledge_id':kid,'decision':decision,'rationale':reason,\n  'transformed_mechanism':'Inherited local relevance scorer; replace occupied-group-uniform mass by observed event fractions, retaining softmax and the complete pooled predictor.' if kid=='paper:din' else 'No new source architecture adopted in this intervention.',\n  'variant_names':['empirical_target','empirical_context','empirical_uniform'] if kid=='paper:din' else [],\n  'nearest_work_difference':'Fixed empirical group masses, no extra parameter/query/view, capacity-matched pooled null and query replacement. Not unnormalized DIN or a reproduction of industry architectures; broader novelty unverified.',\n  'falsifier':'Target readout fails to exceed new empirical-uniform and strongest frozen pooled control, or its gain is matched by the history-query/duplicated-evidence control or reverses under paired repetition.'\n })\nPath('proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(proposal,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Wrote proposal.json with',len(proposal['variants']),'variants,',len(proposal['study']['contrasts']),'contrasts,',len(proposal['knowledge_assessments']),'knowledge assessments.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\nWrote proposal.json with 3 variants, 4 contrasts, 7 knowledge assessments.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,100p' history_g3_r0007_balanced_target.py && tail -n 55 history_g1_r0019_pooled_observed.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,100p' history_g3_r0007_balanced_target.py && tail -n 55 history_g1_r0019_pooled_observed.py\"","aggregated_output":"/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n\"\"\"Equal occupied-match-group mass versus global history retrieval.\n\nFull paired_match features and the hybrid's d-vector feature path are inherited.\nThe new mechanism fixes inter-group weight mass and learns only within groups.\nContext queries remain target independent, but the groups use target matches.\nUniform controls preserve allocated capacity and isolate balancing/extra paths;\ntheir allocated scorer is executed with zero gradient, not active capacity.\nNo training/optimizer/loss/input changes and no measured gain or novelty claim.\n\"\"\"\nimport math\nimport torch\nfrom torch import nn\n\nCONFIG = {'embedding_dim': 16, 'hidden': [128, 64], 'lr': 0.001, 'joint_mode': 'observed', 'statistic_mode': 'count', 'grouping_mode': 'match', 'histogram_grouping': 'match', 'histogram_pairing': 'observed', 'target_query': True, 'separate_reads': True, 'group_balanced': True, 'learned_weights': True}\n\n\nclass Model(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, meta, config=None):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.config = {**CONFIG, **(config or {})}\n        self.target_query = self.config['target_query']\n        self.group_balanced = self.config['group_balanced']\n        self.learned_weights = self.config['learned_weights']\n        self.separate_reads = self.config['separate_reads']\n        if not self.separate_reads:\n            raise ValueError('This study fixes separate field reads')\n        self.joint_mode = self.config['joint_mode']\n        self.statistic_mode = self.config['statistic_mode']\n        self.grouping_mode = self.config['grouping_mode']\n        if self.joint_mode not in ('observed', 'independent'):\n            raise ValueError('Unknown joint_mode')\n        if self.statistic_mode not in ('count', 'rate'):\n            raise ValueError('Unknown statistic_mode')\n        if self.grouping_mode not in ('match', 'rank', 'occupied_global'):\n            raise ValueError('Unknown grouping_mode')\n        # Only the appended retrieval normalization, query and weighting change.\n        # Original learned means and observed count tables remain fixed.\n        if self.grouping_mode != 'match':\n            raise ValueError('This study fixes learned pooling to match')\n        self.histogram_grouping = self.config['histogram_grouping']\n        self.histogram_pairing = self.config['histogram_pairing']\n        if self.histogram_grouping not in ('match', 'rank'):\n            raise ValueError('Unknown histogram_grouping')\n        if self.histogram_pairing not in ('observed', 'independent'):\n            raise ValueError('Unknown histogram_pairing')\n        if (self.joint_mode, self.statistic_mode, self.histogram_grouping,\n                self.histogram_pairing) != ('observed', 'count', 'match', 'observed'):\n            raise ValueError('This study fixes the complete paired_match representation')\n        self.category = meta['category_field_index']\n        self.brand = meta['brand_field_index']\n        dim = self.config['embedding_dim']\n        # Preserve ancestor allocation order and activate its existing scorer.\n        # All four variants allocate identical shapes and compute both weightings.\n        self.embeddings = nn.ModuleList([\n            nn.Embedding(size, dim, padding_idx=0) for size in meta['buckets']\n        ])\n        self.action = nn.Embedding(5, dim, padding_idx=0)\n        self.recency = nn.Embedding(33, dim, padding_idx=0)\n        self.attention = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Linear(dim * 4, 64), nn.PReLU(), nn.Linear(64, 1)\n        )\n        layers = []\n        width = len(meta['fields']) * dim + 4 * dim + 4 + 64 + dim\n        for hidden in self.config['hidden']:\n            layers.extend([nn.Linear(width, hidden), nn.ReLU()])\n            width = hidden\n        layers.append(nn.Linear(width, 1))\n        self.output = nn.Sequential(*layers)\n\n    def _match_counts(self, batch):\n            mask = batch['history_mask']\n            target_c = batch['static'][:, self.category:self.category + 1]\n            target_b = batch['static'][:, self.brand:self.brand + 1]\n            hc = batch['history_category']\n            hb = batch['history_brand']\n            # Zero represents padding/missing; missing-to-missing is never a match.\n            cm = mask & (target_c > 0) & (hc > 0) & (hc == target_c)\n            bm = mask & (target_b > 0) & (hb > 0) & (hb == target_b)\n            n = mask.float().sum(-1)\n            c = cm.float().sum(-1)\n            b = bm.float().sum(-1)\n            joint = (cm & bm).float().sum(-1)\n            independent = c * b / n.clamp_min(1)\n            return n, c, b, joint, independent\n\n    def _statistics(self, counts):\n            n, c, b, joint, independent = counts\n            selected = joint if self.joint_mode == 'observed' else independent\n            if self.statistic_mode == 'count':\n                # Fixed scale from frozen history_limit=128, never from validation.\n                # For fractional independence estimates the same log1p applies.\n                return torch.log1p(torch.stack([n, c, b, selected], -1)) / math.log(129.0)\n            denom = n.clamp_min(1)\n            return torch.stack([\n                (n > 0).float(), c / denom, b / denom, selected / denom\n            ], -1)\n\n    def _membership(self, batch):\n        mask = batch['history_mask']\n        target_c = batch['static'][:, self.category:self.category + 1]\n        }\n        for scope in ('context', 'pooled'):\n            observed, marginal = counts[scope + '_observed'], counts[scope + '_marginal']\n            result[scope + '_channel_margin_error_max'] = (observed.sum(2) - marginal.sum(2)).abs().max()\n            result[scope + '_gap_total_error_max'] = (observed[:, 0] - marginal[:, 0]).abs().max()\n            result[scope + '_nonnegative_violation_max'] = (-marginal).clamp_min(0).max()\n            result[scope + '_subset_violation_max'] = (marginal[:, 1:] - marginal[:, :1]).clamp_min(0).max()\n        norms = []\n        for name, value in counts.items():\n            compact = torch.log1p(value) / math.log(129.0)\n            norms.append((views[name].square().sum(-1) - compact.square().sum((1, 2, 3))).abs().max())\n        result['isometric_lift_norm_error_max'] = torch.stack(norms).max()\n        # These are feature invariances. Full-model logits need not share them.\n        reverse, padded, zero_length = dict(batch), dict(batch), dict(batch)\n        for field in ('history_category', 'history_brand', 'history_type', 'history_age_seconds', 'history_mask'):\n            reverse[field] = batch[field].flip(-1)\n            zero_length[field] = batch[field][:, :0]\n            fill = batch[field].new_zeros((batch[field].shape[0], 2))\n            if field != 'history_mask':\n                fill.fill_(1)\n            padded[field] = torch.cat([batch[field], fill], -1)\n        for label, altered in (('reordering', reverse), ('padding', padded)):\n            result[label + '_feature_error_max'] = (features - self._gap_features(self._gap_tables(altered))).abs().max()\n        result['zero_length_feature_abs_max'] = self._gap_features(self._gap_tables(zero_length)).abs().max()\n        for label, field in (('empty', 'history_mask'), ('missing', 'history_brand'), ('tied', 'history_age_seconds')):\n            altered = dict(batch)\n            altered[field] = torch.zeros_like(batch[field])\n            result[label + '_feature_abs_max'] = self._gap_features(self._gap_tables(altered)).abs().max()\n        changed = dict(batch)\n        changed['static'] = torch.zeros_like(batch['static'])\n        # Constant action merges contexts; unlike a bijective action rename it\n        # can expose the inherited sum-of-products partition dependence.\n        changed['history_type'] = torch.ones_like(batch['history_type'])\n        changed_views = self._association_views(self._gap_tables(changed))\n        result['pooled_target_action_invariance_error_max'] = torch.stack([\n            (views['pooled_' + association] - changed_views['pooled_' + association]).abs().max()\n            for association in ('observed', 'marginal')]).max()\n        applicable = self.category_vocab > 4 and self.brand_vocab > 4\n        result['witness_applicable'] = float(applicable)\n        if applicable:\n            for kind in ('context', 'association'):\n                witness = self._association_witness(batch, kind)\n                witness_counts = self._association_counts(self._gap_tables(witness))\n                witness_views = {name: self._gap_lift(value) for name, value in witness_counts.items()}\n                for name, value in witness_views.items():\n                    result[kind + '_witness_' + name + '_gap_max'] = (value[0] - value[1]).abs().max()\n                added = self.gap_head(witness_views[key]).squeeze(-1)\n                result[kind + '_witness_added_logit_gap'] = (added[0] - added[1]).abs()\n                if kind == 'association':\n                    for scope in ('context', 'pooled'):\n                        margins = witness_counts[scope + '_observed'].sum(2)\n                        result[scope + '_witness_margin_error_max'] = (margins[0] - margins[1]).abs().max()\n                    parent = _ParentModel.forward(self, witness)\n                    result['association_witness_pre_gap_parent_logit_error_max'] = (parent[0] - parent[1]).abs()\n        return {name: float(value) for name, value in result.items()}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport ast, hashlib, json, subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\nruntime=json.loads(subprocess.run(['python3','/workspace/tools.py','resolve','run://r-001'],check=True,capture_output=True,text=True).stdout)\np=json.loads(Path('proposal.json').read_text())\ndef check(value,schema,path='study'):\n typ=schema.get('type')\n types={'object':dict,'array':list,'string':str,'boolean':bool}\n if typ in types: assert isinstance(value,types[typ]),path+' type'\n if 'const' in schema: assert value==schema['const'],path+' const'\n if 'enum' in schema: assert value in schema['enum'],path+' enum'\n if isinstance(value,str): assert len(value)>=schema.get('minLength',0),path+' minLength'\n if isinstance(value,list):\n  assert len(value)>=schema.get('minItems',0),path+' minItems'\n  for i,v in enumerate(value): check(v,schema.get('items',{}),path+f'[{i}]')\n if isinstance(value,dict):\n  for k in schema.get('required',[]): assert k in value,path+' missing '+k\n  props=schema.get('properties',{})\n  if schema.get('additionalProperties') is False: assert not set(value)-set(props),path+' additional properties'\n  for k,v in value.items():\n   if k in props: check(v,props[k],path+'.'+k)\ncheck(p['study'],runtime['study_schema'])\nallowed=set(runtime['context']['allowed_observation_ids'])\nassert p['parent_trial'] in allowed\nassert set(p['study']['evidence_refs'])<=allowed\nassert p['study']['protocol_ref']==runtime['required_study_protocol_ref']\nassert 1<=len(p['variants'])<=4\nassert any(v['role']=='candidate' for v in p['variants'])\nassert len({v['name'] for v in p['variants']})==len(p['variants'])\nbase_ast=None\nfor v in p['variants']:\n file=v['file']; assert Path(file).name==file and file.endswith('.py')\n source=Path(file).read_text(); m=ast.parse(source); compile(m,file,'exec')\n cfg=next(n for n in m.body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='CONFIG' for t in n.targets))\n assert ast.literal_eval(cfg.value)==v['config']\n assert hashlib.sha256(source.encode()).hexdigest() in v['note']\n cfg.value=ast.Constant(None)\n dumped=ast.dump(m,include_attributes=False)\n if base_ast is None: base_ast=dumped\n else: assert dumped==base_ast,'Variant changes beyond CONFIG'\nreviewed=set(runtime['context']['latest_knowledge_usage']['retrieved_ids'])\nassert reviewed <= {a['knowledge_id'] for a in p['knowledge_assessments']}\n# New diagnostics contain a fixed 28 base keys, 10 loop keys and <=7 witness keys.\nmodel=next(n for n in ast.parse(Path('candidate.py').read_text()).body if isinstance(n,ast.ClassDef) and n.name=='Model')\ndiag=next(n for n in model.body if isinstance(n,ast.FunctionDef) and n.name=='diagnostics')\nbase=next(n.value for n in ast.walk(diag) if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='result' for t in n.targets))\nprint('Prospective study schema: PASS')\nprint('Allowed evidence, parent, protocol, unique variant files and roles: PASS')\nprint('CONFIG/source hashes and otherwise-identical variant ASTs: PASS')\nprint('Knowledge coverage: PASS')\nprint('Diagnostic upper bound:',len(base.keys)+10+7,'<=64')\nprint('New training/performance: PENDING HOST (proposal phase)')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
